+## Wake Sessions / Morning Logs Alignment Addendum
+
+This addendum is normative for wake execution and immediate morning logging. It preserves the existing one-morning resolver while adding Wake Session and MorningLog as operational records downstream of resolution.
+
+- The canonical morning resolver owns day meaning, selected mode, wake boundary, resolved wake time, alarm activation, and materialized delivery events.
+- The Wake Session owns execution state for one operational morning: primary alarm, wake checks, awake confirmation, quiet cancellation, expiry, and reconciliation.
+- MorningLog owns factual local records needed for reliability, restoration, and immediate user confirmations. It must not become a parallel day-purpose resolver.
+- These records must remain separate: `suhoorWakeOutcome`, `fastingDayPlanned`, `fastingIntentConfirmed`, `fajrWakeOutcome`, `fajrPrayerOutcome`, and future `fastCompletionOutcome`.
+- Selecting Suhoor sets `fastingDayPlanned` for the resolved morning. Tapping `I’m awake for Suhoor` confirms Suhoor wake and sets `fastingIntentConfirmed` for that morning.
+- Tapping `I’m awake for Fajr` confirms Fajr awake status only. It must not mark Fajr prayer as prayed.
+- Tapping `I prayed Fajr` confirms Fajr prayer outcome only. It must not invent or rewrite Suhoor, fasting, or wake outcomes except where the user action explicitly says so.
+- Lack of awake confirmation may produce `expiredUnconfirmed` or `unconfirmed`. It must not automatically produce `Fajr missed`, `Fast missed`, or prayer judgment.
+- Quiet remains an intentional suppression overlay. It may log `quietMorning`, cancel wake execution, and preserve underlying Fajr/Suhoor meaning, but it must not log a missed prayer or missed fast.
+- Wake Session state must be recomputed or reconciled after mode changes, wake-time changes, date rollover, app relaunch, timezone/location changes, and delivery-ledger discrepancies.
+- Wake Sessions and local operational MorningLogs are core system records for all users. Long-term analytics, streaks, adaptive recommendations, and advanced reporting remain separate future/paid surfaces unless another spec changes that scope.
+
