+## Wake Sessions / Wake Check Delivery Alignment Addendum
+
+This addendum is normative for MVP wake-check delivery and supersedes any lower wording that treats snooze as the primary Subh wake-retry mechanism.
+
+- A Wake Session materializes one primary wake alarm plus eligible wake-check alarms. Wake checks are separate scheduled deliveries, not native snooze for MVP.
+- Default core behavior is one primary alarm plus up to five wake checks at five-minute intervals, for a maximum of six total wake attempts.
+- Fajr wake checks must not be scheduled later than five minutes before Fajr ends.
+- Suhoor wake checks must not be scheduled later than five minutes before Fajr begins.
+- Each Wake Session delivery should carry or deterministically derive: `wakeSessionID`, date key, fire date, mode, role (`primaryWake` or `wakeCheck`), wake-check sequence number, sound role, and schedule signature.
+- Platform identifiers for primary and wake-check alarms must be deterministic and scoped so stale wake checks can be cancelled without affecting unrelated dates or events.
+- Lock Screen actions for Wake Session alarms should expose `Stop` and `Open Subh`. The `Open Subh` action routes to the relevant in-app confirmation CTA.
+- Stopping or dismissing one AlarmKit alarm stops only that occurrence. It must not mark the user awake and must not cancel later wake checks by itself.
+- When the user taps `I’m awake for Fajr` or `I’m awake for Suhoor`, delivery must cancel any pending primary alarm and all remaining wake checks for that Wake Session.
+- When the user confirms Quiet during an active Wake Session, delivery must cancel all remaining primary/wake-check alarms for that session and report `notScheduledBecauseQuiet` or the equivalent structured quiet status.
+- Mode changes, wake-time commits, time/location/timezone changes, and resolver boundary changes must cancel stale Wake Session alarm identifiers and schedule only the corrected eligible set.
+- Reconciliation must detect missing, stale, duplicate, or mismatched wake-check deliveries, not only primary alarms.
+- Advanced wake-check intervals, adaptive wake checks, and heavy-sleeper escalation are out of this MVP delivery pass unless another approved spec explicitly requests them.
+
